{"skill":{"slug":"python-executor","displayName":"Python Executor"},"version":{"version":"0.1.5","createdAt":1771403346215,"changelog":"- Added detailed documentation in SKILL.md, including usage examples, input schema, and pre-installed library list.\n- Clarified environment specs, supported triggers, and output file handling.\n- Listed practical use cases for web scraping, data analysis, image/video/3D processing, API calls, PDF generation, and automation.\n- Provided quick start instructions and links to related skills and official documentation.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6346,"sha256":"92928f9f1ba888b6e01014ce25d18dfda678293254761f6e7a292ef4dc212a10","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2517,"sha256":"017a09791a3fb799f7a69351e4369ba5b06dc9ea475ccc31e437bfdaab2edf83","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789036526027,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5e8fc2c62dd9ec2bacb1ab5ce05ca1b29c79a8996c9af00915f9543c8f99b58e","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5e8fc2c62dd9ec2bacb1ab5ce05ca1b29c79a8996c9af00915f9543c8f99b58e","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: python-executor\nVersion: 0.1.5\n\nThe skill allows the AI agent to execute arbitrary Python code within a sandboxed environment via `infsh app run`. The `allowed-tools: Bash(infsh *)` permission is broad, granting the agent the ability to execute any `infsh` command. While the `SKILL.md` claims a 'safe sandboxed environment' and does not contain explicit malicious instructions for the agent, the inherent capability to execute arbitrary code (even if sandboxed) and the broad `infsh` permissions present a significant risk if the agent were to be compromised via prompt injection, potentially leading to the execution of malicious Python code or other `infsh` commands.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161807677},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":64,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789036526027},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is purpose-aligned for sandboxed Python execution, but its documented installation path asks users to run mutable remote code directly in a shell.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network-capable libraries and examples are coherent for this purpose, including requests and API-call examples, but users should treat any executed code as able to contact external services and return generated files.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The quick start documents curl -fsSL https://cli.inference.sh | sh && infsh login, which executes a remote installer before local inspection or independent verification of the installer itself; the note about binary checksum verification partially mitigates but does not remove that risk.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The routing description is broad and includes general triggers such as python, automation, API calls, and web scraping, which could cause a code-execution skill to be selected for more tasks than necessary.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact claims no elevated permissions or background processes, and no bundled persistence mechanism or local executable scripts were present in the inspected artifact; the main privilege concern is the remote CLI installer executing with the invoking user's account privileges.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to run Python code through inference.sh, and the allowed tool scope is limited to Bash invocations matching infsh commands; the examples align with data processing, scraping, media generation, and API-call use cases.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. The Python execution feature is coherent, but do not run the curl-to-shell quick start unless you trust inference.sh's installer delivery path. Prefer a separately downloaded, inspected, and verified CLI installer, and avoid sending secrets or private data through executed Python code unless you intend that code to contact external services.","findings":"[SC2] unexpected: The remote CLI installation is related to using the service, but the pipe-to-shell pattern is an avoidable high-impact supply-chain risk and supports Review.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad triggers are expected for a general Python executor, but they increase the chance of accidental invocation for a high-impact code-execution workflow.\n[SQP-2] expected: Networking is purpose-aligned for scraping and API calls, but the artifact does not prominently warn that user code may send data to external services.\n[E1] expected: The GitHub API call is a benign example of outbound HTTP use, not evidence of hidden exfiltration.\n[RP1] unexpected: The related-skill npx examples are optional, but they use mutable unpinned references and add supply-chain exposure beyond the core Python executor.\n[T03] unexpected: The static finding is supported by the artifact's quick-start installer command and is the primary basis for the Review verdict.\n[T08] unexpected: The static finding about unpinned related-skill installation is supported by the artifact, though it is secondary because those commands are optional examples.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789036526027}}}}}